# Normalise to LF in the repository and on checkout.
#
# Without this, a clone on Windows checks out install.sh with CRLF endings, and bash then fails
# with `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M` for anyone who copies that file to a Mac or Linux
# box. The generator already writes LF; this makes git stop helpfully undoing that.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell is happy with either, but CRLF is what a Windows editor will produce anyway, so
# declaring it prevents a spurious whole-file diff the first time someone edits it there.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
